{"notes":"Reframing from Mark: stating the gap is not a confession, it is an invitation. A limit named precisely enough becomes a work item for standards bodies, vendors and government programmes rather than an apology. Write this section so it is FILLABLE — name what a filler would have to provide, not merely what persona cannot do.

His prediction for what fills it, and it is convincing: 'the CAC card is still plugged in', most of the time. That answer is already deployed at scale under HSPD-12, and it beats a FIDO2 tap on the axis that matters here, because card removal is an event rather than an expiry guess. It also works for a non-technical reason worth recording in the spec: the CAC is simultaneously the building badge and the photo ID, so a physical and social constraint keeps it with the human. No protocol supplies that.

So the section should distinguish limits that are genuinely unfillable (coercion) from limits that are unfilled BY THIS DAEMON and invite an answer (continuity of presence, binding to intent). Conflating the two would discourage exactly the contribution it should attract."}
